### =====================================================
### Register - POST /account/register
### Self-register (anónimo, no requiere Authorization).
### Reglas server-side: RoleId siempre 1001; si no viene
### subdivisionId se crea una nueva (requiere operatorId)
### y el usuario queda AccessLevel 2; con subdivisión
### válida queda AccessLevel 20.
### =====================================================

### Test 1: Registro con subdivisión existente (happy path) — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "johndoe.register@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123",
  "email": "johndoe.register@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+50255551234",
  "accessLevelId": 20,
  "roleId": 1001,
  "name": "Juan Pérez",
  "operatorId": 307,
  "organizationId": 229,
  "divisionId": 192,
  "subdivisionId": 336
}

### Test 2: Registro sin subdivisión (se crea una nueva; requiere operatorId) — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "janedoe.register@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123",
  "email": "janedoe.register@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+50255555678",
  "accessLevelId": 2,
  "roleId": 1001,
  "name": "Jane Pérez",
  "operatorId": 307,
  "organizationId": 229,
  "divisionId": 192
}

### Test 3: Sin organizationId — 400 (ORGANIZATION_REQUIRED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "sinorg.register@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123",
  "email": "sinorg.register@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+50255550000",
  "accessLevelId": 20,
  "roleId": 1001,
  "operatorId": 307
}

### Test 4: Username ya existente — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "johndoe.register@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123",
  "email": "johndoe.register@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+50255551234",
  "accessLevelId": 20,
  "roleId": 1001,
  "operatorId": 307,
  "organizationId": 229,
  "divisionId": 192,
  "subdivisionId": 336
}

### Test 5: Campo requerido faltante (sin password) — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "sinpass.register@example.com",
  "email": "sinpass.register@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+50255559999",
  "accessLevelId": 20,
  "roleId": 1001,
  "organizationId": 229
}

### Test 6: Organización sin licencias disponibles — 409 (LICENSES_EXHAUSTED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "sinlicencia.register@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123",
  "email": "sinlicencia.register@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+50255558888",
  "accessLevelId": 20,
  "roleId": 1001,
  "operatorId": 307,
  "organizationId": 999999999,
  "divisionId": 1,
  "subdivisionId": 1
}
